# L §7.1: the cap counts the digits of the reduced fraction's numerator and denominator, not of its decimal
# expansion, and L §2.4 prints an exact value as its shortest exact decimal.  0.5^5000 = 1/2^5000: a 1 506-digit
# denominator (under the cap), printed with 5 000 decimals.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input h: num
input n: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  h = 0.5
  n = 5000

ask q: pow(h, n)
=== expect
q: 0.000 ...
  cut 2026-12-31
